Include relations.

Let R, S be relation.

Lemma: for all x, y. R[x,y] and S is symmetric implies S[y,x].
Proof:
    Fix x.
    Fix y.
    Assume R[x,y] and S is symmetric.
    Then S[y,x] by symmetry.
    Hence S[y,x].
qed.

Lemma: for all x, y. R[x,y] implies S[x,y].
Proof:
    Fix x.
    Fix y.
    Assume R[x,y].
    Then S[x,y] by transitivity.
    Hence S[x,y].
qed.
